[{"text": "The assembly will hear an address by her", "start": 0.32, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "Excellency", "start": 2.88, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "Jessica Rose Epel Alupo,", "start": 4.72, "duration": 6.52}, {"text": "Vice President of the Republic of", "start": 8.68, "duration": 3.96}, {"text": "Uganda.", "start": 11.24, "duration": 3.8}, {"text": "I request protocol to escort her", "start": 12.64, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "Excellency and invite her to address the", "start": 15.04, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "assembly.", "start": 18.2, "duration": 2.6}, {"text": ">> The President of the UN General", "start": 31.12, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "Assembly,", "start": 32.599, "duration": 3.881}, {"text": "Excellencies, the heads of state and", "start": 34.56, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "government,", "start": 36.48, "duration": 3.32}, {"text": "the Secretary General of the United", "start": 38.16, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Nations, distinguished delegates, ladies", "start": 39.8, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "and gentlemen,", "start": 42.4, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "I wish to bring you warm greetings from", "start": 44.4, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "His Excellency General Yoweri Kaguta", "start": 46.68, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "Museveni,", "start": 49.6, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "President of the Republic of Uganda,", "start": 51.12, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "on whose behalf", "start": 54.52, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "I am delivering this statement.", "start": 56.6, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "And the statement reads as follows.", "start": 59.72, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "I wish to express my gratitude for the", "start": 62.76, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "invitation extended to me to address", "start": 65.08, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "this 81st session", "start": 67.76, "duration": 6.2}, {"text": "of the United Nations General Assembly.", "start": 70.12, "duration": 6.84}, {"text": "I have been unable to attend in person", "start": 73.96, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "and delegated her Excellency Major", "start": 76.96, "duration": 6.84}, {"text": "Retired Jessica Alupo Rose Epel,", "start": 79.6, "duration": 6.84}, {"text": "Vice President of the Republic of Uganda", "start": 83.8, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "to represent me.", "start": 86.44, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "I congratulate His Excellency Dr. Csaba", "start": 88.92, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "K\u0151r\u00f6si Rahman on your election as", "start": 91.48, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "President of the 81st session of the UN", "start": 95.24, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "General Assembly", "start": 97.92, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "and assure you of Uganda's full support.", "start": 99.52, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "I also thank His Excellency", "start": 103.44, "duration": 6.2}, {"text": "Her Excellency Miss Anna Lena Baerbock", "start": 106.08, "duration": 7.48}, {"text": "for her stewardship of the 80th session", "start": 109.64, "duration": 7.68}, {"text": "and wish to thank the Secretary General,", "start": 113.56, "duration": 6.2}, {"text": "His Excellency Antonio Guterres for his", "start": 117.32, "duration": 5.32}, {"text": "unwavering commitment to the United", "start": 119.76, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "Nations.", "start": 122.64, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 124.479, "duration": 4.121}, {"text": "80 years ago,", "start": 126.36, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "the United Nations was established in", "start": 128.6, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "the aftermath of the Second World War to", "start": 131.52, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "foster international cooperation and", "start": 134.36, "duration": 6.52}, {"text": "prevent future armed conflicts.", "start": 137.6, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "As we convene here today, we must", "start": 140.88, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "confront the reality of living in very", "start": 143.92, "duration": 6.6}, {"text": "uncertain times shadowed by the", "start": 147.6, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "persistent threat of global conflict.", "start": 150.52, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "It is imperative that we work together", "start": 154.04, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "to avert warfare.", "start": 157.48, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "We must reflect on the founding", "start": 160.28, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "principles of the UN Charter and", "start": 162.76, "duration": 6.84}, {"text": "recommit ourselves to saving succeeding", "start": 165.64, "duration": 7.48}, {"text": "generations from the scourge of war,", "start": 169.6, "duration": 6.28}, {"text": "reaffirming faith in fundamental human", "start": 173.12, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "rights and the dignity of human person,", "start": 175.88, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "ensuring equal rights for all large", "start": 179.28, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "nations and small, establishing", "start": 181.64, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "conditions for justice and respect for", "start": 184.84, "duration": 5.72}, {"text": "international law, and promoting social", "start": 187.56, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "progress alongside better standards of", "start": 190.56, "duration": 4.679}, {"text": "life.", "start": 193.8, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "Uganda family believes that", "start": 195.239, "duration": 4.441}, {"text": "multilateralism and international", "start": 197.36, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "cooperation", "start": 199.68, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "remain the most vital mechanisms for", "start": 201.2, "duration": 6.039}, {"text": "addressing our shared challenges.", "start": 204.08, "duration": 6.52}, {"text": "Accordingly, we remain and reaffirm our", "start": 207.239, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "commitment to the principles of the UN", "start": 210.6, "duration": 5.96}, {"text": "Charter as the cornerstone of global", "start": 213.48, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "diplomacy,", "start": 216.56, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "supporting the interconnected pillars of", "start": 218.16, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "peace and security,", "start": 220.88, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "human rights, humanitarian affairs, and", "start": 223.12, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "sustainable development.", "start": 226.72, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "We believe the United Nations must", "start": 229.36, "duration": 6.52}, {"text": "remain agile and adaptive to evolving", "start": 231.88, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "global realities.", "start": 235.88, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "Uganda is committed to working with the", "start": 238.44, "duration": 6.04}, {"text": "entire membership to build consensus on", "start": 240.72, "duration": 7.48}, {"text": "necessary systemic reforms, particularly", "start": 244.48, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "within the UN Security Council.", "start": 248.2, "duration": 6.28}, {"text": "We call for a comprehensive reform to", "start": 251.04, "duration": 6.12}, {"text": "render the Council more equitable,", "start": 254.48, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "transparent, democratic, and", "start": 257.16, "duration": 4.12}, {"text": "representative.", "start": 259.44, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "In this regard, we demand Africa's", "start": 261.28, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "rightful representation", "start": 264.28, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "in both the permanent and non-permanent", "start": 266.52, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "categories to correct historical", "start": 269.56, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "imbalances in line with the common", "start": 272.16, "duration": 6.12}, {"text": "African position articulated in the", "start": 274.919, "duration": 6.801}, {"text": "Ezulwini Consensus and the Sirte", "start": 278.28, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "Declaration.", "start": 281.72, "duration": 6.04}, {"text": "Regarding the ongoing UN aid initiative,", "start": 284.04, "duration": 6.6}, {"text": "Uganda commends efforts to streamline", "start": 287.76, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "the UN system to make it cost-effective,", "start": 290.64, "duration": 6.76}, {"text": "efficient, and well-coordinated.", "start": 293.919, "duration": 7.161}, {"text": "However, these reform processes must not", "start": 297.4, "duration": 8.08}, {"text": "dilute agreed UN mandates, commitments,", "start": 301.08, "duration": 8.2}, {"text": "and programs, nor should they impede the", "start": 305.48, "duration": 8.439}, {"text": "implementation of the 2030 agenda.", "start": 309.28, "duration": 6.36}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 313.919, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "when we adopted the 2030 agenda for", "start": 315.64, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "SDGs,", "start": 318.48, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "the 17 SDGs", "start": 320.68, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "in 2015,", "start": 323.08, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "we committed to leaving no one behind.", "start": 325.0, "duration": 7.32}, {"text": "Yet, progress remains elusive with only", "start": 328.56, "duration": 8.96}, {"text": "36% of the 139 targets currently on", "start": 332.32, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "track.", "start": 337.52, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Numerous obstacles hinder our efforts to", "start": 339.04, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "accelerate progress, key among being", "start": 342.08, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "limited physical space.", "start": 345.44, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "many developing countries lack", "start": 347.88, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "sufficient financial resources to fund", "start": 349.72, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "their development needs with a", "start": 352.76, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "disproportionate share of revenues", "start": 355.16, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "directed towards debt servicing rather", "start": 357.84, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "than critical public infrastructure", "start": 360.96, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "and social services.", "start": 363.68, "duration": 5.88}, {"text": "This challenge requires urgent reform of", "start": 366.44, "duration": 6.12}, {"text": "international financial architecture to", "start": 369.56, "duration": 6.2}, {"text": "afford developing nations a stronger", "start": 372.56, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "voice in decision-making", "start": 375.76, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "alongside the full implementation of the", "start": 378.4, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "Sevilla commitment of the pact for the", "start": 381.44, "duration": 4.92}, {"text": "future.", "start": 384.72, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "Furthermore, equitable taxation is", "start": 386.36, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "essential for mobilizing domestic", "start": 389.44, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "resources.", "start": 392.12, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "An inclusive international tax system is", "start": 393.6, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "critical for strengthening global", "start": 396.8, "duration": 5.88}, {"text": "cooperation, curbing illicit financial", "start": 399.28, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "flows and addressing profit shifting by", "start": 402.68, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "multinational corporations.", "start": 406.64, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "Mr. President, Uganda fully supports the", "start": 409.88, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "ongoing intergovernmental negotiation", "start": 413.64, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "on the United Nations Framework", "start": 416.84, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Convention on international tax", "start": 418.72, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "cooperation and its protocols on", "start": 421.08, "duration": 5.88}, {"text": "cross-border services and tax dispute", "start": 423.88, "duration": 5.88}, {"text": "resolution, and we urge all member", "start": 426.96, "duration": 7.959}, {"text": "states to negotiate constructively.", "start": 429.76, "duration": 8.76}, {"text": "Uganda has commended the implementation", "start": 434.919, "duration": 6.961}, {"text": "of its fourth national development plan", "start": 438.52, "duration": 6.28}, {"text": "as part of our national strategy to", "start": 441.88, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "accelerate economic transformation", "start": 444.8, "duration": 6.119}, {"text": "and achieve sustainable development.", "start": 447.88, "duration": 5.48}, {"text": "This strategy is anchored on four", "start": 450.919, "duration": 5.561}, {"text": "high-impact growth pillars, including", "start": 453.36, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "agro-industrialization,", "start": 456.48, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "tourism development, mineral", "start": 458.64, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "exploitation, and science, technology,", "start": 461.2, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "and innovation.", "start": 464.32, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Our goal is to drive double-digit growth", "start": 466.24, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "over the 5-year period and ultimately", "start": 469.52, "duration": 8.8}, {"text": "grow our economy tenfold to a GDP of 500", "start": 472.56, "duration": 9.56}, {"text": "billion US dollars by 2040,", "start": 478.32, "duration": 6.76}, {"text": "creating jobs and enhancing the quality", "start": 482.12, "duration": 6.76}, {"text": "of life of all Ugandans.", "start": 485.08, "duration": 7.56}, {"text": "Mr. President, distinguished delegates,", "start": 488.88, "duration": 6.76}, {"text": "the peaceful resolution of conflicts", "start": 492.64, "duration": 6.279}, {"text": "through diplomacy is indispensable for", "start": 495.64, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "sustainable peace, security, and", "start": 498.919, "duration": 5.081}, {"text": "economic growth.", "start": 502.08, "duration": 4.839}, {"text": "Most conflicts arise from unresolved", "start": 504.0, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "local and regional grievances and demand", "start": 506.919, "duration": 6.441}, {"text": "comprehensive politically led and", "start": 510.4, "duration": 6.28}, {"text": "locally owned solutions rather than", "start": 513.36, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "purely military responses.", "start": 516.68, "duration": 6.799}, {"text": "Uganda remains a consistent contributor", "start": 520.24, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "to regional stability,", "start": 523.479, "duration": 4.761}, {"text": "particularly in the Horn of Africa and", "start": 525.68, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "the Great Lakes region, and our security", "start": 528.24, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "approach is rooted in a Pan-African", "start": 531.36, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "framework that seeks peace through", "start": 534.0, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "collective alliances and regional", "start": 536.64, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "cooperation.", "start": 539.76, "duration": 3.28}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 541.36, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "investing in a healthy population", "start": 543.04, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "remains a core strategic priority for", "start": 545.96, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Uganda.", "start": 548.8, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Under NDP 4, we are expanding health", "start": 550.52, "duration": 6.6}, {"text": "investments to ensure accessible,", "start": 554.0, "duration": 6.2}, {"text": "affordable, and equitable health care", "start": 557.12, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "across the country.", "start": 560.2, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "This includes modernizing health", "start": 562.2, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "centers, upgrading regional referral", "start": 564.2, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "hospitals, and integrating digital", "start": 567.0, "duration": 5.4}, {"text": "health solutions to improve service", "start": 569.64, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "delivery and accountability.", "start": 572.4, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "We are actively addressing the dual", "start": 576.04, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "burden of communicable", "start": 578.48, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "and non-communicable diseases and our", "start": 580.8, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "responses to HIV AIDS combine strong", "start": 584.0, "duration": 6.12}, {"text": "political leadership with sustained", "start": 587.36, "duration": 5.96}, {"text": "community involvement keeping Uganda on", "start": 590.12, "duration": 7.6}, {"text": "track to achieve the UNAIDS 95-95-95", "start": 593.32, "duration": 7.52}, {"text": "targets and contribute to end the ending", "start": 597.72, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "AIDS as a public health threat", "start": 600.84, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "by 20 30.", "start": 603.8, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "Having successfully contained outbreaks", "start": 606.84, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "such as the Bundibugyo Ebola virus", "start": 609.32, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "Uganda has built a resilient public", "start": 613.28, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "health framework.", "start": 615.88, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "We call upon development partners and", "start": 617.52, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "multilateral institutions", "start": 620.56, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "to bridge financing gaps, enhance", "start": 623.04, "duration": 7.08}, {"text": "pandemic preparedness, and ensure", "start": 626.56, "duration": 7.32}, {"text": "equitable access to diagnostic tools,", "start": 630.12, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "medicines, and vaccines worldwide.", "start": 633.88, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "As the chair of NAM, Uganda continues to", "start": 638.12, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "uphold the principles of unity, peace,", "start": 641.64, "duration": 7.84}, {"text": "and solidarity among developing nations.", "start": 645.16, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "We remain dedicated to advancing the", "start": 649.48, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "international covenant on the right to", "start": 652.2, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "development aiming to transform the 1986", "start": 655.08, "duration": 5.8}, {"text": "declaration", "start": 659.24, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "into a binding operational instrument", "start": 660.88, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "that tackles structural global", "start": 664.04, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "inequalities.", "start": 666.32, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "We look forward to hosting the ministers", "start": 668.04, "duration": 5.96}, {"text": "of NAM member states and observers at", "start": 670.64, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "the ministerial meeting of the NAM", "start": 674.0, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "Coordinating Bureau in Kampala from", "start": 676.64, "duration": 8.199}, {"text": "December 2nd to 4th, 2026.", "start": 679.56, "duration": 7.84}, {"text": "Mr. President as [snorts] the selection", "start": 684.839, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "process for next for the next UN", "start": 687.4, "duration": 5.16}, {"text": "Secretary General progresses", "start": 689.8, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "Uganda has presented a candidate in the", "start": 692.56, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "name of Ambassador Olara Otunnu.", "start": 695.88, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "Ambassador Olara Otunnu brings over four", "start": 699.6, "duration": 6.44}, {"text": "decades of distinguished service across", "start": 702.76, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "the UN system, international diplomacy,", "start": 706.04, "duration": 7.08}, {"text": "and public administration.", "start": 709.76, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "As the inaugural Special Representative", "start": 713.12, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "for Children and Armed Conflict", "start": 715.52, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "1998-2005,", "start": 718.0, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "he placed the protection of war-affected", "start": 720.72, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "children firmly on the on the Security", "start": 723.68, "duration": 6.76}, {"text": "Council agenda and established the", "start": 727.28, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "monitoring and reporting mechanism under", "start": 730.44, "duration": 7.84}, {"text": "resolution 1612 in 2005.", "start": 734.28, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "His extensive experience, statesmanship,", "start": 738.28, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "and proven capacity for", "start": 742.04, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "consensus-building", "start": 743.72, "duration": 5.08}, {"text": "make him exceptionally qualified to lead", "start": 745.8, "duration": 6.84}, {"text": "the Secretariat at this critical time.", "start": 748.8, "duration": 6.76}, {"text": "As I conclude, Mr. President,", "start": 752.64, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "for eight decades, the United Nations", "start": 755.56, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "has stood as a central pillar of", "start": 758.56, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "international peace, human rights, and", "start": 760.92, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "development.", "start": 763.68, "duration": 3.56}, {"text": "While acknowledging its vital", "start": 765.24, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "achievements and convening power, we", "start": 767.24, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "must continue to reform the organization", "start": 770.68, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "to ensure it becomes more transparent,", "start": 773.88, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "cost-effective,", "start": 777.4, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "efficient, and representative.", "start": 778.92, "duration": 5.0}, {"text": "Through renewed international", "start": 782.08, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "cooperation, the UN can truly deliver on", "start": 783.92, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "its founding promises for all humanity.", "start": 787.44, "duration": 8.72}, {"text": "I thank you for your kind attention.", "start": 791.36, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": ">> On behalf of the Assembly, I wish to", "start": 801.52, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "thank the Vice President of the Republic", "start": 804.08, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "of Uganda.", "start": 806.48, "duration": 2.84}]